---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Reveal from '../components/Reveal.tsx';
---

<BaseLayout title="Methods — VIOT Research">
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <Reveal>
      <p class="kicker mb-4">Methodology</p>
      <h1 class="heading-academic text-5xl md:text-6xl leading-tight">
        Framework Architecture
      </h1>
      <p class="text-academic mt-6 text-xl max-w-3xl">
        The Virtual Ion-Optics Testbed (VIOT) progressed through four phases. The production results are driven by the VIOT-3 (Axisymmetric) and VIOT-4 (3D + DSMC) frameworks.
      </p>
    </Reveal>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 border-t border-edge">
    <Reveal>
      <h2 class="heading-academic text-3xl mb-8">Phase III: VIOT-3 (Axisymmetric)</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
        <div class="text-academic space-y-4">
          <p>
            VIOT-3 is the production framework for the core erosion campaign. It models the barrel erosion mode (axisymmetric, inside aperture wall).
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Poisson Solver:</strong> SuperLU direct factorization (replaces non-convergent Red-Black SOR from VIOT-2).</li>
            <li><strong>Plasma Push:</strong> True leapfrog with backward half-kick for stable E-field integration.</li>
            <li><strong>Sputter Yield:</strong> 2D (Energy, θ) bilinear interpolation capturing geometric shadowing.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-panel border border-edge p-6 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto text-navy">
          // 15 critical defects from Phase II corrected
          // Defect 3: Post-CEX velocity
          // Old: v = 0
          // New: Maxwellian sampling at 400 K

          // Defect 5: MCC double-counting
          // Old: spurious collisions
          // New: exact null-collision ratio
        </div>
      </div>
    </Reveal>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 border-t border-edge">
    <Reveal>
      <h2 class="heading-academic text-3xl mb-8">Phase IV: VIOT-4 (3D + DSMC)</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
        <div class="text-academic space-y-4">
          <p>
            VIOT-4 extends the framework to 3D to capture pit-and-groove erosion on the downstream face and interstitial web.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>DSMC Collision:</strong> No-Time-Counter (NTC) acceptance <code>P = σ·g·dt/V_cell</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Poisson Operator:</strong> Corrected Laplacian assembly (interior diag +6, off-diagonals -1, residual 1.7e−11).</li>
            <li><strong>MD Pipeline:</strong> LAMMPS AIREBO crystalline MD for graphene substrate interactions.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-panel border border-edge p-6 rounded-lg text-sm">
          <h3 class="font-sans font-bold text-ink mb-3">Verification Fixes (Adversarial Review)</h3>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-academic">
            <li>MD projectile velocity unit conversion (1e-12 → 1e-2). 300 eV Xe verified at 210 Å/ps.</li>
            <li>Sputter count isolated to type-1 (C) atoms.</li>
            <li>Engine reinject modified to refill only inactive slots, preserving mid-flight ions.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Reveal>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
